    q: "A hotel already has a professional operator. What does the owner's asset manager add?",
    a: "It adds the owner's view. The operator is paid mostly on revenue and spends the owner's money, so the asset manager holds it to account for profit: approving budgets and capital, challenging pricing and costs, benchmarking results and enforcing the contracts. It also makes the owner's own decisions: financing, tax appeals, brand strategy and when to sell.",
