    q: "Wage rates at your hotel will rise 6% next year. How should you and the operator respond?",
    a: "Offset it with productivity rather than cuts guests will notice. Schedule to forecast demand, cut overtime and agency staff, cross-train, share managers with nearby hotels and simplify service where brand standards allow, such as lighter stayover cleaning or shorter outlet hours. Recover the rest through rate where possible, and track hours per occupied room and guest scores together.",
